WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:12.592
"I'm super excited about our sleepover with the kids from People Place," Winnie said to Ben.

2
00:00:12.593 --> 00:00:19.407
It was Monday morning at Monster Academy, and the two friends had just signed up for the welcome committee.

3
00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:22.784
"Me too," Ben said. "I can't wait!"

4
00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:29.485
"Hey, guess what?" Cleo ran over to them. "I just joined the welcome committee too!"

5
00:00:29.486 --> 00:00:33.551
"Awesome," Ben said. "We'll have lots of fun."

6
00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:39.613
Winnie nodded. "We need to come up with ideas to make the people feel really welcome.

7
00:00:39.614 --> 00:00:46.963
Mr. Freaky said about ten students are coming, plus three parent chaperones and Mayor Hubbletree."

8
00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:52.415
Ben laughed. "Is the mayor actually going to sleep here?

9
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:57.124
That would make Mr. Freaky really, um, freaked out."

10
00:00:57.125 --> 00:01:01.837
"I think he just wants to make sure things go well," Winnie said.

11
00:01:01.838 --> 00:01:05.674
"Some human parents are worried about their kids sleeping here.

12
00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:09.316
Apparently they think monsters are dangerous."

13
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:20.312
A huge monster with sharp claws lumbered by, growling and blowing smoke from his nostrils.

14
00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.856
Cleo waved to him.

15
00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:26.365
"Hey, Rudy!" Then she turned back to Winnie and Ben.

16
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:31.542
"That's silly. Everyone knows humans are way scarier than monsters."

17
00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:34.293
"It's ridiculous," Ben agreed.

18
00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:40.185
"Ar-ooo!" Lon howled as he came zipping down the hallway on a skateboard.

19
00:01:40.186 --> 00:01:44.287
"Yo, dudes!" he said. "Check out this new trick I—oof!"

20
00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:47.204
Lon crashed into Cleo.

21
00:01:47.205 --> 00:01:49.483
"Ouch!" she cried.

22
00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:54.120
Lon's skateboard flew through the air and hit a locker. Bam!

23
00:01:54.121 --> 00:01:58.098
"Ahh!" Mr. Freaky cried, racing toward them.

24
00:01:58.099 --> 00:02:01.802
"Another accident!" He glared at the werewolf.

25
00:02:01.803 --> 00:02:04.762
"Lon! How many times do I have to tell you?

26
00:02:04.763 --> 00:02:07.460
No skateboarding in the halls.

27
00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:11.234
It's not safe, and you keep damaging school property.

28
00:02:11.235 --> 00:02:17.519
Look at this locker! It's dented, and now Mr. Bog will have to fix it."

29
00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.942
Lon stood up and rubbed his elbow.

30
00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:26.012
"Sorry, Mr. Freaky," he mumbled, grabbing his skateboard and hurrying off.

31
00:02:26.013 --> 00:02:28.820
Cleo turned back to Ben and Winnie.

32
00:02:28.821 --> 00:02:32.886
"So what do we need to do to get ready for the sleepover?"

33
00:02:32.887 --> 00:02:38.685
Winnie tapped her chin. "We mostly need ideas for decorations and snacks."

34
00:02:38.686 --> 00:02:42.721
"We could cook special treats," Cleo said.

35
00:02:42.722 --> 00:02:46.551
"Like slime cakes and grilled bat wings."

36
00:02:46.552 --> 00:02:49.302
"Yum!" Winnie said.

37
00:02:49.303 --> 00:02:52.104
"I love slime cakes," Ben said.

38
00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:55.348
"But I'm not sure humans like to eat monster food."

39
00:02:55.349 --> 00:03:03.774
He remembered the humans' first visit to the Monster Academy cafeteria, which had ended in disaster.

40
00:03:03.775 --> 00:03:05.825
"They like pizza though. We could make—"

41
00:03:05.826 --> 00:03:10.047
"Hey, Jen!" Winnie called. "Watch where you're going!"

42
00:03:10.048 --> 00:03:13.939
Jen was staring at her phone as she walked down the hallway.

43
00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.752
Francis was bent over, picking up a book.

44
00:03:16.753 --> 00:03:20.520
Jen nearly stepped on the worm monster.

45
00:03:20.521 --> 00:03:25.032
"Oops!" Jen cried. "Sorry about that, Francis!"

46
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.979
"I'm fine," Francis said.

47
00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.227
"But last week a slime monster was running down the hallway and smooshed me.

48
00:03:32.228 --> 00:03:34.652
I stayed flat for hours!"

49
00:03:34.653 --> 00:03:37.181
Mr. Freaky slapped his forehead.

50
00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:40.745
"Students, you need to stay alert when you're in the hallway.

51
00:03:40.746 --> 00:03:46.010
What's going on around here?" he moaned.

52
00:03:46.011 --> 00:03:50.396
"Nobody is paying attention to safety rules anymore!"

53
00:03:50.397 --> 00:03:56.468
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

54
00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:02.327
Ben noticed that Jen looked upset. "Is something wrong, Jen?"

55
00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:06.568
Jen sighed. "It's the sleepover.

56
00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:10.870
Dave wants to come, but his mom thinks monsters are dangerous.

57
00:04:10.871 --> 00:04:14.158
He's worried that she won't let him participate."

58
00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:18.903
"She thinks monsters are dangerous?" Cleo rolled her eyes.

59
00:04:18.904 --> 00:04:26.068
"It was humans, not monsters, who locked my uncle Tut in a museum display!"

60
00:04:26.069 --> 00:04:35.319
Mr. Bog was standing on a ladder nearby, repairing a hole in the ceiling that some students had made while playing with a spiked ball.

61
00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:41.714
"I agree, Cleo," he said. "Monsters are no more dangerous than people."

62
00:04:41.715 --> 00:04:45.197
"Try telling Dave's mom that," Jen said.

63
00:04:45.198 --> 00:04:50.901
"She's one of the chaperones who's planning to inspect our school building before the sleepover.

64
00:04:50.902 --> 00:04:56.694
And if she doesn't like what she sees . . ." Jen swallowed hard.

65
00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:00.673
"That's it—Dave won't be here."

66
00:05:00.674 --> 00:05:07.004
"Don't worry. Our school will be ready for the sleepover," Mr. Bog promised.

67
00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:11.694
"I fixed the kitchen stoves this morning, and they're working great.

68
00:05:11.695 --> 00:05:14.186
Now I'm patching holes in the ceiling.

69
00:05:14.187 --> 00:05:18.135
Once I'm done here, I'll fill in the big sinkhole in the parking lot.

70
00:05:18.136 --> 00:05:23.165
Tomorrow I'll wash all the windows."

71
00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:26.637
"Wow, Mr. Bog," Winnie said sympathetically.

72
00:05:26.638 --> 00:05:32.991
"You're busy. It sounds like Monster Academy needs two custodians."

73
00:05:32.992 --> 00:05:39.121
"I've got a list of tasks longer than a witch's broom, but I'll get it done before the big day arrives."

74
00:05:39.122 --> 00:05:42.956
Mr. Bog stretched his arm up to reach the hole.

75
00:05:42.957 --> 00:05:47.802
His ladder wobbled as he filled the hole with smelly swamp plaster.

76
00:05:47.803 --> 00:05:55.064
Ben smiled. "Thanks to Mr. Bog, Dave's mom is going to be really impressed when she inspects the school."

77
00:05:55.065 --> 00:05:57.488
"When is she coming?" Winnie asked.

78
00:05:57.489 --> 00:06:03.600
"Wednesday," Jen said. "Thanks, guys. I feel a little better now that—"

79
00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:09.583
"Uh-oh!" Mr. Bog tumbled off the ladder.

80
00:06:09.584 --> 00:06:16.277
The bucket of swamp plaster landed on his head!

